    "note": "Amended version (with House Committee Amendments 2-22-2017), not enrolled; the House passed it 2017-02-28 and later amendments are not in the text read. The print has stray amendment markers. Section 3 (77-36-1.1) adds an enhancement when the domestic violence was committed while carrying a firearm or dangerous weapon, and Section 4 (77-36-5.1) has the court require surrender of firearms and ammunition and federal-ban notice; those lines are garbled by the markers so not quoted. Section 4 also changes \"may\" to \"shall\" for the protective-order condition."
